{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואחרי כן יצא אחיו", :translit "v'acharei khen yatza achiv", :gloss "And after that came out his brother"} {:he "כן", :translit "khen", :gloss "thus / so"} {:he "ע' אומות", :translit "shiv'im umot", :gloss "seventy nations"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כן", :b "ע"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 10 lists seventy nations descended from Noah's three sons, traditionally understood as the full catalogue of peoples in the world (Genesis 10:1-32). Jacob, father of the twelve tribes of Israel, stands outside this enumeration; his descendants constitute a people set apart from the seventy.", :sources ["Genesis 10:1-32"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וידו", :translit "veyado", :gloss "and his hand"} {:he "וידו הנטויה", :translit "veyado hanetuyah", :gloss "and his hand stretched out"} {:he "וידו חלקתה להם", :translit "veyado chelkatah lahem", :gloss "and his hand portioned to them"} {:he "בישעיה במפלת העכו\"ם", :translit "b'Yeshayah b'miflat ha-akum", :gloss "in Isaiah at the downfall of the nations"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וידו" "וידו הנטויה" "וידו חלקתה להם"]}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 26 describes the downfall of adversaries, using imagery of an outstretched hand: 'YHWH has sent out His hand' (Isaiah 26:11, 'וידו הנטויה' in the Masoretic phrasing of the passage). Jacob's hand grasping Esau's heel at birth (Genesis 25:26) foreshadows the future subjugation of Esau's descendants, understood within the broader prophetic vision in Obadiah 1:18 and Malachi 1:2-3 of Jacob's dominance over Esau.", :sources ["Isaiah 26:11" "Genesis 25:26" "Obadiah 1:18" "Malachi 1:2-3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "כן", :a-value 70, :b "ע", :b-value 70, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וידו" "וידו הנטויה" "וידו חלקתה להם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וידו", :refs ["Genesis 25:26" "Isaiah 14:27" "Isaiah 34:17" "Ezekiel 1:8" "Job 5:18" "Lamentations 3:53"],